ittle bit  bigger than that and then the closings  are another story Sam's Club which is  the company's warehouse division or  membership club retailer division has  been struggling for a while now it has  been losing ground to Costco and look  retail is really tough right now this  company is in retail warfare and so that  is part of what's happening there which  is separate the other problems that tax  bill is that it would create jobs so on  that front  not happening what Walmart's a big  employer how does this affect it does it  affect other employers well walmart sort  of sets the tone in terms of what it  does with its wages and and not so long  ago it was not doing these things with  wages so this does send a message and  again I think also on the benefits side  of things it's not just about wages and  the other argument there though is we're  in a very tight labor market now so all  companies are under pressure to raise  wages simply from a competitive  standpoint but Walmart is the number one  private company employer two point three  million employees of 1.5 million in the  US alone and this for that reason is is  significant Walmart says they hope to  place some of these employees at the  Sam's Club at other stores what's the  likelihood that that could happen  that could happen I mean it is such a  big company it could absorb those  employees the other thing that's  happening is it's taking I think about  ten maybe up to twelve of those Sam's  Clubs and repurposing them as  distribution fulfillment centers for  e-commerce which is what's happening  retailers are in this position now they  have all this real estate and people are  buying online they're trying desperately  to really make it possible for you to  get your products as fast as you can and  fulfillment centers are a big part of  the puzzle there so those fulfillment  centers will obviously need employees so  it's unclear how many people will be  impacted by the Sam's Club news the gala  girl al